# CITY SURFER Art Direction

Look: stylized & saturated "city flood surrealism" at sunset. Alto's Odyssey polish, but urban.
NOT photorealistic. Clean shapes, bold color, chunky readable foam.

Signature contrast: warm orange light vs. cool teal water. Every scene must read as
"orange sky above, teal water below, warm rim light on everything".

Canonical palette (linear-space intent — tune via `ArtDirection.swift` / uniforms, not scattered magic numbers):
- Sky zenith:    deep dusk blue   `#2B3A67`
- Sky horizon:   hot orange       `#FF7A3C`
- Sun disc:      near-white gold  `#FFE8B0`
- Water deep:    dark teal        `#0A3A4A`
- Water shallow: bright turquoise `#2EC4B6`
- Foam:          warm white       `#FFF6E9`
- Buildings:     warm concrete    `#C9A27E` (sun side) / cool blue-grey `#5C6B85` (shadow side)
- Neon accents:  magenta `#FF3E8A` and cyan `#38E5FF`, used sparingly

When changing look: update `Render/ArtDirection.swift` and mirror literals in `Shaders.metal` in the same change.

## Technical rules
- Render HDR: offscreen `rgba16Float` scene target → bloom in HDR → ACES-style tonemap in the final composite (never tonemap in sky/solid/wave fragments).
- Lighting: one directional "sun" low on the horizon + sky ambient (hemisphere: orange from horizon, blue from zenith).
- Fog is WARM (mix toward horizon orange, never grey).
- Prefer cheap stylized tricks (gradients, fresnel, rim light, vertex animation) over expensive physically-correct techniques. Target: 60 fps (ideally 120) on iPhone, portrait.
- Never break the existing MTL4 frame pacing / residency set setup. Every new buffer or texture must be added to the residency set.
- Water: no shadow-map receive — soft edge darkening / stylized tricks only.
- After meaningful look changes: `make device-build` and compare a device screenshot to the art reference.
